1
00:00:00,668 --> 00:00:02,043
HEY.
HEY.

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:04,797
WOW. YOU LOOK NICE;
WHAT'S THE OCCASION?

3
00:00:04,797 --> 00:00:06,966
MONICA AND I ARE CELEBRATING
OUR TEN-MONTH ANNIVERSARY.

4
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:08,843
GOT RESERVATIONS
AT JEAN-GEORGES.

5
00:00:08,843 --> 00:00:11,219
WELL... HOW'D YOU
GET IN THERE?

6
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:13,012
AH, MADE A FEW CALLS,
PULLED SOME STRINGS

7
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:14,723
AND THEY AGREED
TO SEAT US AT 11:30

8
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:16,391
IF WE BOTH HAD THE CHICKEN
AND DIDN'T GET DESSERT.

9
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:18,101
I SEE.

10
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:21,104
( knocking )

11
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,815
HI, CHANDLER.
HEY, CAITLIN.

12
00:00:22,815 --> 00:00:24,859
SOMEBODY GOT A HAIRCUT.
UGH. I HATE IT.

13
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:26,819
I LOOK LIKE AN
EIGHT-YEAR-OLD BOY.

14
00:00:26,819 --> 00:00:28,403
YEAH, WELL, IF THAT WAS TRUE,
GYM CLASS WOULD HAVE BEEN

15
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:29,488
A LOT MORE INTERESTING.

16
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:31,615
( chuckles )

17
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:35,118
IT'S, UH, $27 EVEN.

18
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:36,871
OH, OKAY. THERE YOU GO.
( duck quacking )

19
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:39,080
HEY, WHERE'S THE CHICKEN?
OH, HE'S IN THE BACK.

20
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,333
THE DUCK PISSED HIM OFF--

21
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:43,377
SAID THAT EGGS CAME FIRST.

22
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,086
THANKS. I'LL
SEE YOU LATER.

23
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,045
OKAY, BYE.

24
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:52,219
WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?

25
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:54,179
WHAT?
THE FLIRTING.

26
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:55,848
AREN'T YOU SUPPOSED TO BE GOING
OUT WITH-- UH, I DON'T KNOW--

27
00:00:55,848 --> 00:00:58,600
HMM, LET'S SEE--
MY SISTER?!

28
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,768
I WAS NOT FLIRTING.

29
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,937
IT WAS TOTALLY FLIRTING.

30
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:03,313
"SOMEBODY GOT A HAIRCUT."

31
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:04,857
( talking gibberish )

32
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:10,153
OKAY, FIRST OF ALL,
THE IMPRESSION? UNCANNY.

33
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,488
AND SECOND, THAT WAS
NOT FLIRTING. THAT WAS

34
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,323
JUST CASUAL CONVERSATION
BETWEEN TWO PEOPLE;

35
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,324
THAT IS ALL.

36
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,159
YEAH, RIGHT.

37
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,412
YOU WANT TO SEE FLIRTING?
I'LL SHOW YOU FLIRTING.

38
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:21,040
I'M GOOD. I'M GOOD.

39
00:01:27,922 --> 00:01:32,801
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

40
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,054
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

41
00:01:35,054 --> 00:01:37,723
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

42
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:42,603
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

43
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:44,897
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

44
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:47,524
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

45
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:51,361
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

46
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,154
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

47
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:56,283
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

48
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:58,201
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

49
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:01,371
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

50
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:05,166
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

51
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,594
I AM SO PROUD OF JOEY.

52
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:17,262
I CAN'T BELIEVE HE'S GOING
TO BE ON LAW AND ORDER.

53
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:18,806
I KNOW, BUT
DON'T YOU THINK

54
00:02:18,806 --> 00:02:21,809
THAT IT SHOULD BE
CALLED "ORDER AND LAW"?

55
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:24,352
NO, BECAUSE FIRST THEY ARREST
THE GUY, AND THEN THEY TRY HIM.

56
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:26,229
YEAH, DON'T GET ME
STARTED ON THAT.

57
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:28,774
I WAS NOT FLIRTING.

58
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:31,526
AND ON YOUR ANNIVERSARY--
FOR SHAME.

59
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:33,070
Rachel:
WHAT'S GOING ON?

60
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:35,489
CHANDLER WAS HITTING
ON THE HOT DELIVERY GIRL.

61
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:39,118
I WAS NOT AND,
OH, GOD, SHH!

62
00:02:39,118 --> 00:02:40,911
WELL, I'M SORRY,
BUT YOU WERE, OKAY?

63
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:43,204
AND BESIDES, IF ANYONE
SHOULD BE HITTING ON HER

64
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,456
IT'S THE GUY
WHO'S SINGLE, OKAY?

65
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,792
THE GUY WHO CAN DO
SOMETHING ABOUT IT.

66
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:51,170
SOUNDS LIKE SOMEONE WANTS
TO BE MR. PIZZA DELIVERY GIRL.

67
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,923
WELL...
IS THAT WHAT
THIS IS ABOUT?

68
00:02:52,923 --> 00:02:56,259
YOU LIKE CAITLIN?

69
00:02:56,259 --> 00:03:00,139
( chuckling ):
ROSS, WE BROKE UP
TWO YEARS AGO.

70
00:03:00,139 --> 00:03:01,890
YOU'VE BEEN MARRIED
SINCE THEN.

71
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:04,309
I THINK IT'S OKAY THAT
WE SEE OTHER PEOPLE.

72
00:03:05,936 --> 00:03:08,229
WELL, I WAS WATCHING HER
THE OTHER DAY

73
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:10,858
AT THE PIZZA PLACE,
AND SHE WAS JUST SO SEXY

74
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:13,944
AND FUNNY AND HAS
THE CUTEST LITTLE...

75
00:03:13,944 --> 00:03:17,238
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?
WE DON'T NEED HER MEASUREMENTS.

76
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:19,491
OKAY, PEPPERONI,
PEPPERONI, PEPPERONI.

77
00:03:19,491 --> 00:03:21,160
ROSS, I KNOW SHE'S PRETTY
AND YOU LOVE HER

78
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,704
BUT IS SHE STUPID?

79
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:25,706
SHE FORGOT MY VEGETARIAN.

80
00:03:25,706 --> 00:03:28,207
THIS IS PERFECT.

81
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:30,377
SHE'LL HAVE TO COME BACK HERE
WITH YOUR PIZZA

82
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:35,090
AND, WHEN SHE DOES, I WILL TURN
ON THE CHARM-O'-ROSS.

83
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:38,177
OH, I AM SO GLAD
YOU DON'T EAT MEAT.

84
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:41,889
SEE? VEGETARIANISM
BENEFITS EVERYONE.

85
00:03:41,889 --> 00:03:43,557
HEY, EVERYBODY,
LOOK WHO'S HERE.

86
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:44,933
YOU REMEMBER
MY GRANDMOTHER?

87
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,060
All: HI!
BUONA SERA.

88
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:48,311
BIG NIGHT.
YEAH, IT'S SO COOL.

89
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:50,731
SO, JOEY ON LAW AND ORDER--
YOU MUST BE VERY PROUD.

90
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:53,608
CHANDLER, SHE DOESN'T
UNDERSTAND A WORD OF ENGLISH.

91
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:56,195
I'M SORRY. I THOUGHT YOU WERE
JOEY'S OTHER GRANDMOTHER.

92
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,115
I'VE DONE IT AGAIN.

93
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:04,244
NO, NONNI--
NONNI'S MY BIGGEST FAN.

94
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,620
YEAH, SHE'S THE ONLY ONE
IN THE FAMILY

95
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,997
WHO'S ALWAYS BELIEVED IN ME.

96
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:09,290
SI, NONNI?
IO SONO NUMERO UNO, NO?

97
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:11,626
( Italian accent ):
SI, BIG STAR.

98
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:14,796
MY BIG FAT JOEY STAR.

99
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:18,675
( chuckles )

100
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:21,887
YEAH, I WEIGHED, LIKE, 27 POUNDS
WHEN I WAS BORN.

101
00:04:23,889 --> 00:04:26,600
HEY, HAPPY ANNIVERSARY.

102
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,268
HAPPY ANNIVERSARY,
TEN MONTHS.

103
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:30,645
OH...

104
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:32,313
SO, UM, WHEN I
WAS IN THE SHOWER

105
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,191
I WAS THINKING ABOUT
OUR FIRST NIGHT IN LONDON.

106
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:36,276
OH, JOEY'S GRANDMOTHER'S
RIGHT THERE.

107
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:37,903
IS THAT THE ONE WHO
SPEAKS ENGLISH OR
THE ONE WHO DOESN'T?

108
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,613
THE ONE WHO DOESN'T.

109
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,907
THAT WAS SOME HOT LOVE
YOU GAVE ME.

110
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,450
I'M GOING TO GO GET READY.

111
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:45,244
HEY, WHY DON'T YOU WEAR
THOSE EARRINGS I GOT YOU?

112
00:04:45,244 --> 00:04:46,703
OH, THAT'S A GREAT IDEA.

113
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,829
I WAS SAVING THEM
FOR SOMETHING SPECIAL.

114
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,039
OKAY.

115
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,500
YOU'VE GOT TO GO HOME.

116
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,254
BUT I LIKE IT HERE.

117
00:04:55,254 --> 00:04:57,714
YOU GOT TO GO HOME
AND GET THE EARRINGS THAT
YOU BORROWED FROM ME, OKAY?

118
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:58,966
CHANDLER WANTS ME
TO WEAR THEM TONIGHT.

119
00:04:58,966 --> 00:05:00,675
OKAY. I THINK
THEY'RE IN MY PURSE.

120
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,010
WHY DON'T YOU GO GET DRESSED?
AND I'LL LOOK FOR THEM.

121
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,720
GREAT.
OKAY.

122
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,099
RACH, HI.

123
00:05:07,099 --> 00:05:08,809
I NEED THOSE EARRINGS
YOU BORROWED.

124
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:13,605
OH, UM... OKAY.

125
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:14,689
YEAH. I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

126
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:17,609
OKAY.

127
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,611
SCUSA, SIGNORA.

128
00:05:19,611 --> 00:05:21,320
( speaking Italian )

129
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,572
NIENTE, GRAZIE.

130
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:23,740
( speaks Italian )

131
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,492
( giggles )

132
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:27,161
WOW, PHEEBS,
YOU SPEAK ITALIAN?

133
00:05:27,161 --> 00:05:28,411
I GUESS SO.

134
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,708
THERE YOU GO.
THANK YOU.

135
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:35,043
WAIT, RACH.
WHERE'S THE OTHER ONE?

136
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:38,463
OH, WHAT?
YOU WANT BOTH OF THEM?

137
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:41,049
RACHEL KAREN GREEN,
WHERE IS THE OTHER EARRING?

138
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,926
OKAY, OKAY. OKAY, LOOK,
JUST DON'T FREAK OUT

139
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:44,303
BUT I KIND OF LOST IT.

140
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:45,637
I KNOW IT'S
IN THE APARTMENT

141
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:48,015
BUT I DEFINITELY LOST IT.

142
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,808
WHAT AM I GOING TO TELL MONICA?

143
00:05:49,808 --> 00:05:51,559
SHE WANTS TO WEAR THEM TONIGHT.

144
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:53,728
I DON'T KNOW. TELL HER
TO WEAR HER OWN EARRINGS.

145
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:55,147
THESE ARE 
HER EARRINGS.

146
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:57,607
NO, NO!

147
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:59,193
YOU LENT ME
MONICA'S EARRINGS?!

148
00:05:59,193 --> 00:06:02,779
I'M NOT ALLOWED
TO BORROW HER STUFF!

149
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:03,780
WHY NOT?

150
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,282
BECAUSE I LOSE HER STUFF!

151
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:13,207
He left a little
after 2:00.

152
00:06:13,207 --> 00:06:15,125
OKAY, NOW, YOU SEE
THAT BLIND GUY RIGHT THERE?

153
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:18,045
I'M GOING TO BASH
HIS HEAD IN LATER.

154
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:19,921
DOV'E, JOEY?
DOV'E, JOEY?

155
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,673
MY BIG SCENE'S COMING UP.

156
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:23,382
THE BIG SCENE COMING UP.

157
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:25,344
IF YOU SAID,
"BIG LIMA BEAN BUBBLING UP"

158
00:06:25,344 --> 00:06:26,970
WOULD SHE UNDERSTAND
THE DIFFERENCE?

159
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,558
RACH, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING?

160
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:33,310
OH, I-I JUST CAN'T WATCH.

161
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:36,313
IT'S TOO SCARY.

162
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:38,606
IT'S A DIAPER
COMMERCIAL.

163
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:42,027
OH, YEAH, WELL, YOU KNOW ME
AND BABIES... RESPONSIBILITIES.

164
00:06:42,027 --> 00:06:44,112
( mock scream )

165
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:45,113
( knock at door )

166
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,198
Caitlin:
PIZZA DELIVERY!

167
00:06:46,198 --> 00:06:48,491
I'LL GET IT!
I WILL GET THAT!

168
00:06:51,703 --> 00:06:52,829
HI.
HI.

169
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:54,497
ONE VEGETARIAN PIZZA.

170
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,749
IT'S $12.15.

171
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:58,335
OH. UH, BY THE WAY

172
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:00,461
IF IT MAKES YOU
FEEL ANY BETTER

173
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,714
I HAPPEN TO LIKE
EIGHT-YEAR-OLD BOYS.

174
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:08,636
WHAT?

175
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:10,013
( stuttering ):
NO... OH, I MEAN...

176
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:12,266
THE, UH... YOUR
HAIR... BEFORE...

177
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:13,975
YOUR HAIR... YOU
SAID YOU THOUGHT

178
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:16,436
THAT YOUR HAIR LOOKED LIKE
AN EIGHT-YEAR-OLD BOY'S

179
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,980
AND I'M, I'M JUST
SAYING, I LIKE IT--

180
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:22,401
THE-THE HAIR.

181
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:24,403
OH. THANKS.

182
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:31,159
YOU UNDERSTAND I DON'T ACTUALLY
LIKE EIGHT-YEAR-OLD BOYS.

183
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,372
YOU KNOW, ALL I'M
LOOKING FOR IS THE MONEY.

184
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:38,250
HERE YOU GO. NOW, STOP
BRINGING US PIZZAS, YOU.

185
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,918
I'M GOING TO TRY.

186
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:42,170
BYE.

187
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,589
( sighs )
YOU'RE WELCOME.

188
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:47,217
YOU COULDN'T LET ME
HAVE HER, COULD YOU?

189
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,218
WHAT?

190
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:49,469
THIS IS A GIRL
I REALLY LIKE

191
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:52,431
AND YOU, YOU HAD
TO SWOOP IN THERE!

192
00:07:52,431 --> 00:07:53,472
WHAT'S GOING ON?

193
00:07:53,472 --> 00:07:54,849
CHANDLER WAS TOTALLY FLIRTING

194
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:58,186
WITH THE HOT DELIVERY GIRL.

195
00:07:58,186 --> 00:07:59,562
THANK YOU FOR THAT.

196
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,899
I WAS NOT FLIRTING.

197
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,025
IT'S OKAY. I DON'T CARE.

198
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,026
IT'S FINE.

199
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:07,321
REALLY?
REALLY?

200
00:08:07,321 --> 00:08:08,322
IT'S NO BIG DEAL.

201
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:09,572
I DO IT ALL THE TIME.

202
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:12,200
( chuckles )

203
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,493
SO, UH...
( clears throat )

204
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,996
YOU-YOU-YOU FLIRT
WITH GUYS ALL THE TIME?

205
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:18,790
SURE. IT DOESN'T
MEAN ANYTHING.

206
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:20,792
JUST LIKE I KNOW
IT DOESN'T MEAN
ANYTHING WITH YOU.

207
00:08:20,792 --> 00:08:22,002
OKAY, BUT THERE'S
A BIG DIFFERENCE, ALL RIGHT?

208
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:23,420
YOU ARE A LOT HOTTER
THAN I AM.

209
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:26,631
TRUE STORY.

210
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,008
CHANDLER, THIS
ACTUALLY BOTHERS YOU?

211
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:29,259
YES, IT DOES BOTHER ME.

212
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:30,802
I THINK IT'D BOTHER
A LOT OF PEOPLE.

213
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:32,762
RACHEL, WHEN YOU WERE
GOING OUT WITH ROSS

214
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,514
DID IT BOTHER YOU
WHEN HE FLIRTED
WITH OTHER WOMEN?

215
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,850
UH, NO. NO,
IT BOTHERED ME

216
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:39,353
WHEN HE SLEPT
WITH OTHER WOMEN.

217
00:08:43,106 --> 00:08:46,193
AND THANK YOU FOR THAT.

218
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:48,111
BUT, YOU KNOW, I NEVER REALLY
HAD ANYTHING TO WORRY ABOUT.

219
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:50,530
ROSS WAS NEVER VERY GOOD
AT THE FLIRTING THING.

220
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:53,492
WHA-WHA...?

221
00:08:53,492 --> 00:08:54,701
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

222
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,119
IT WORKED WITH YOU.

223
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,038
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?
NO, YOU'RE RIGHT.

224
00:08:58,038 --> 00:09:00,207
WE MET, YOU FLIRTED
AND THEN BAM!

225
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:02,667
NINE YEARS LATER,
YOU HAD ME.

226
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:05,045
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.

227
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:06,380
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M GOING TO DO?

228
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,631
I AM GOING TO ORDER
ANOTHER PIZZA

229
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,467
AND WHEN CAITLIN GETS HERE

230
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:12,719
YOU-- I WILL SHOW YOU
HOW WELL I FLIRT.

231
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:13,928
IN FACT, I WILL--

232
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:15,596
I WILL GET
HER PHONE NUMBER--

233
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:19,184
WELL...
AND NOT THE ONE
ON THE MENU.

234
00:09:21,853 --> 00:09:23,730
I FOUND IT.
( gasps ):
OH, THANK GOD!

235
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:25,564
WHERE WAS IT?
ON YOUR DRESSER.

236
00:09:25,564 --> 00:09:28,026
OKAY, THAT IS THE ONE
WE ALREADY HAVE.

237
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:29,194
OH!

238
00:09:29,194 --> 00:09:30,445
OKAY, HERE'S
MY BIG SCENE.

239
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:31,779
MY BIG SCENE'S HERE.

240
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:33,865
What do you bet,
nobody heard anything?

241
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:35,450
No bet.

242
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:37,869
Anybody home?

243
00:09:37,869 --> 00:09:39,329
OH, MY GOD.

244
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:40,455
WHAT?

245
00:09:40,455 --> 00:09:42,207
OKAY, EVERYBODY
JUST KEEP SMILING.

246
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:44,792
IT'LL KILL MY GRANDMOTHER
IF SHE FINDS OUT.

247
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:45,877
WHAT IS IT?

248
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:48,838
THEY CUT ME OUT
OF THE SHOW.

249
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:51,341
WHAT?
ARE YOU SURE?

250
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:53,176
MAYBE YOUR SCENE'S
COMING UP.

251
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:56,304
NOT LIKELY, 'CAUSE YOU SEE
THAT BODY BAG RIGHT THERE?

252
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,722
YEAH.
I'M IN IT.

253
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:05,564
THIS IS TERRIBLE.
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

254
00:10:05,564 --> 00:10:08,942
I DON'T KNOW. THIS LITTLE
OLD LADY LIVES FOR MY CAREER.

255
00:10:08,942 --> 00:10:12,320
WHEN THEY DUMPED ME OFF DAYS
OF OUR LIVES, SHE ALMOST DIED.

256
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,696
THAT'S NOT GOOD.

257
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:14,822
YOU'RE NOT SMILING.
NOT THAT FACE.

258
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:17,784
SMILE. EVERYBODY SMILE!

259
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:19,619
JOEY, WHY DON'T YOU
JUST TELL HER WHAT HAPPENED?

260
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:22,330
I MEAN, IT'S NOT YOUR FAULT.
IF WE KEEP TALKING THIS WAY,

261
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:25,333
AREN'T WE GOING
TO FREAK HER OUT SOON?

262
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,586
( speaking Italian )

263
00:10:27,586 --> 00:10:29,463
OH, UH, UH, SOON. SOON.

264
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,464
I'M GOING TO BE ON SOON.

265
00:10:30,464 --> 00:10:31,756
I... THERE I AM!

266
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,800
I'll let you know.

267
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,801
Grandma:
NO!

268
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,928
SAM WATERSTON.

269
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:39,389
NO, NO, NO. THAT'S...
THAT'S ME. THAT'S ME.

270
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:41,641
NO. SAM WATERSTON.

271
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:44,644
CRIME MISDEMEANOR,
CAPRICORN ONE...

272
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:48,398
SHE DOESN'T KNOW "HELLO,"
BUT SHE KNOWS CAPRICORN ONE.

273
00:10:48,398 --> 00:10:49,816
PHOEBE?
HMM?

274
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:51,610
I HAVE TO HAVE
THOSE EARRINGS.

275
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:53,612
WE'RE GOING TO LEAVE
AS SOON AS THE SHOW'S OVER.

276
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:55,071
BUT I ALREADY
GAVE THEM BACK TO YOU.

277
00:10:57,491 --> 00:10:59,242
NO, YOU DIDN'T.

278
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:00,994
ALL RIGHT, I ALREADY
DIDN'T GAVE THEM BACK TO YOU.

279
00:11:00,994 --> 00:11:02,245
THAT'S WHAT I SAID.

280
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:06,416
RACHEL, WHERE IS
THAT OTHER EARRING?

281
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:08,543
IT'S NOT HERE, PHEEBS.
IT'S NOT HERE.

282
00:11:08,543 --> 00:11:10,670
OH! I WENT TO JOEY
AND CHANDLER'S LAST NIGHT.

283
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,423
OKAY. MAKE SURE YOU CHECK
CHANDLER'S JEWELRY BOX.

284
00:11:15,509 --> 00:11:17,636
WAIT A MINUTE. WHAT?
CHANDLER HAS A JEWELRY BOX?

285
00:11:17,636 --> 00:11:19,887
OKAY, WE HAVE,
LIKE, TEN MINUTES.

286
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:21,431
DO YOU WANT ME
TO GET INTO THAT NOW?

287
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:28,313
HEY, PHEEBS.

288
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:29,981
HOW'S THAT, UH...

289
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:33,276
VEGETARIAN PIZZA
WORKING OUT FOR YOU, HUH?

290
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,695
YOU AND
THOSE VEGETABLES

291
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:40,074
HAVE A REAL THING 
GOING ON, HUH?

292
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:43,995
WHY ARE YOU BEING WEIRD?

293
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,208
DO YOU LIKE IT?

294
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:53,254
NO. THAT WOULD BE,
"WHY ARE YOU BEING CUTE?"

295
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:55,382
OKAY, I'M WORKING
ON MY FLIRTING.

296
00:11:55,382 --> 00:11:57,758
OH! I DID NOT GET THAT.

297
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:02,222
SO, MONICA, DO YOU...
DO YOU LIKE THE LAW &amp; ORDER?

298
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:03,848
YEAH. IT'S GOOD.

299
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:05,225
SEE, I'M FINDING OUT
ALL THIS STUFF ABOUT YOU TODAY--

300
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:06,601
LIKE YOU LIKE
THE LAW &amp; ORDER

301
00:12:06,601 --> 00:12:07,935
AND-AND YOU FLIRTED

302
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,854
WITH EVERY GUY IN
THE TRISTATE AREA.

303
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,189
SHH! SHH!

304
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:12,357
ALL RIGHT.

305
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:14,859
OKAY, LET ME
GET THIS STRAIGHT.

306
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:17,945
IT'S OKAY FOR YOU TO FLIRT,
BUT NOT FOR ME.

307
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,615
OH, I'M SO GLAD
WE CLEARED THAT UP.

308
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:22,450
LOOK, I'M SORRY, BUT
SOME THINGS ARE DIFFERENT

309
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,578
FOR MEN AND FOR WOMEN.

310
00:12:24,578 --> 00:12:26,454
GO ON, TEACH ME SOMETHING
ABOUT MEN AND WOMEN.

311
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:27,997
OKAY, I'VE ALREADY
TAUGHT YOU SO MUCH ALREADY,

312
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,291
BUT WHATEVER...

313
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:31,876
SEE, WHEN YOU
FLIRT WITH A GUY

314
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,628
YOU THINK, "I'M JUST
FLIRTING. NO BIG DEAL."

315
00:12:33,628 --> 00:12:35,213
BUT THE GUY
IS THINKING "FINALLY,

316
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:37,382
SOMEBODY WHO WANTS
TO SLEEP WITH ME."

317
00:12:37,382 --> 00:12:38,717
NO WAY!

318
00:12:38,717 --> 00:12:40,218
IT'S TRUE.

319
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:42,845
THAT'S PATHETIC.
AGAIN, TRUE.

320
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,889
( scoffs ) 
AND THIS GOES
FOR ALL GUYS?

321
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:47,392
ALL GUYS THAT ARE AWAKE.

322
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:48,893
THEN WE GO TO SLEEP.

323
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:50,270
AND ALL GUYS FROM
THE OTHER END OF THE WORLD

324
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:51,938
WAKE UP AND BEHAVE
THE EXACT SAME WAY.

325
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,858
ALL RIGHT, IT'S
ANOTHER COMMERCIAL

326
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,277
AND I STILL
HAVEN'T TOLD HER.

327
00:12:57,277 --> 00:13:00,238
JOEY, THIS IS, LIKE,
THE LAST COMMERCIAL.

328
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,615
YOU GOT, LIKE,
TEN MINUTES LEFT.

329
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:04,618
I KNOW, I KNOW.
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO? OH!

330
00:13:04,618 --> 00:13:05,868
NO, YOU ARE NOT
GOING TO RUN OUT

331
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:07,036
AND LEAVE HER HERE.

332
00:13:09,456 --> 00:13:11,625
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

333
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:12,584
OH!

334
00:13:15,587 --> 00:13:17,046
JOEY?

335
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:19,299
UH... JOEY'S GOING
TO BE RIGHT BACK.

336
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:21,134
RIGHT... BACK.

337
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,885
( chuckles )

338
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,971
MEANWHILE, LET'S, LET'S,
LET'S TALK ABOUT YOU.

339
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:29,350
SO... YOU'RE OLD AND SMALL.

340
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:37,816
DID YOU FIND IT?

341
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:39,026
THE EARRING? NO.
BUT, LOOK--

342
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,654
I FOUND MY SUNGLASSES
UNDER THE COUCH.

343
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:43,281
I'VE BEEN LOOKING FOR THESE
SINCE, LIKE, LAST SUMMER.

344
00:13:43,281 --> 00:13:44,991
OKAY, THOSE ARE
MY SUNGLASSES.

345
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:47,826
YOU BORROWED
THEM FROM ME.

346
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:50,079
OKAY. CALM DOWN.
HERE THEY ARE.

347
00:13:51,122 --> 00:13:52,499
PHOEBE?

348
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,543
WHAT DO I DO?

349
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:57,587
I DON'T KNOW.
I DON'T KNOW.

350
00:13:57,587 --> 00:13:59,464
ALL RIGHT. WELL...

351
00:13:59,464 --> 00:14:01,007
WE'RE JUST GOING TO HAVE
TO TELL MONICA, THAT'S ALL.

352
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:04,803
OH, GOD, SHE'S
GOING TO KILL ME.

353
00:14:04,803 --> 00:14:07,096
I SUPPOSE I COULD TELL HER
IT WAS JUST ALL MY FAULT.

354
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,807
OH, THAT
WOULD BE GREAT.

355
00:14:11,476 --> 00:14:13,353
MON, CAN I TALK
TO YOU FOR A SEC?

356
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:14,813
YEAH. WHAT IS IT?

357
00:14:14,813 --> 00:14:18,525
UM... I LOST ONE
OF YOUR EARRINGS.

358
00:14:18,525 --> 00:14:21,486
I'M SORRY.
I AM SO, SO SORRY.

359
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:24,863
WOW...

360
00:14:24,863 --> 00:14:26,825
ALL RIGHT. WELL, I MEAN...

361
00:14:26,825 --> 00:14:28,743
WHAT CAN YOU DO?
IF YOU LOST IT, YOU LOST IT.

362
00:14:28,743 --> 00:14:31,538
I'LL REPLACE IT, I PROMISE.
I FEEL SO TERRIBLE.

363
00:14:31,538 --> 00:14:33,623
ALL RIGHT, SWEETIE, THAT'S FINE.
YOU DIDN'T DO IT ON PURPOSE.

364
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:34,791
NO.

365
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:36,876
LOOK AT YOU.
COME HERE.

366
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,587
AW...

367
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:43,341
IS THAT BETTER?
YEAH. YOU'RE THE BEST.

368
00:14:43,341 --> 00:14:46,302
OKAY, WAIT A MINUTE.

369
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:47,887
WAIT A MINUTE. I-I-I...
I CAN'T DO THIS.

370
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:49,389
LISTEN, HONEY, THIS IS...

371
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:50,849
IT'S NOT PHOEBE'S FAULT.

372
00:14:50,849 --> 00:14:52,809
SHE LENT ME 
THE EARRINGS.

373
00:14:52,809 --> 00:14:55,019
I LOST IT.
I'M SO SORRY, HONEY.

374
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:57,938
I FEEL TERRIBLE, TOO.

375
00:14:57,938 --> 00:15:00,525
THAT IS EXACTLY
WHY I DO NOT
LEND YOU STUFF!

376
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:03,069
OKAY?

377
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:05,905
FIRST, IT'S MY JEWELRY!
IF IT'S NOT MY JEWELRY,
IT'S MY BLUE SWEATER!

378
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,699
IF IT'S NOT
MY BLUE SWEATER,
IT'S MY SUNGLASSES!

379
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:09,409
YOUR SUNGLASSES?

380
00:15:09,409 --> 00:15:10,577
YES!

381
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:11,911
OH, RIGHT.

382
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,246
( knocking on door )

383
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,874
PIZZA!
MINE! MINE! MINE!

384
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:18,835
OKAY, HERE GOES.

385
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:22,296
PREPARE YOURSELVES
FOR SOME CLASS "A" FLIRTING.

386
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,215
OKAY, HOLD ON.

387
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:25,675
OKAY.

388
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,553
HEY, YOU HAVE
NOTHING TO PROVE.

389
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:30,263
AND IF YOU REALLY LIKE THIS GIRL

390
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:31,598
I DON'T THINK FLIRTING'S
THE RIGHT WAY TO...

391
00:15:31,598 --> 00:15:34,100
UH! UH! UH! UH! UH!

392
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,227
YOU'LL SEE. OKAY.

393
00:15:38,855 --> 00:15:40,732
WH-WHAT'S HER NAME?

394
00:15:40,732 --> 00:15:42,024
All:
CAITLIN.

395
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:44,151
CAITLIN.

396
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,824
( giggling )

397
00:15:49,824 --> 00:15:51,492
HEY!

398
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:54,245
OH, WE... WE CAN'T
KEEP EATING LIKE THIS.

399
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:58,792
IT'S, UH.... $12.50.

400
00:15:58,792 --> 00:16:01,294
OKAY. UM...

401
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,796
SO...

402
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:06,925
DO YOU...
MAKE THE PIZZAS

403
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:11,011
IN ONE OF THOSE, UH...
WOOD-BURNING OVENS?

404
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:14,140
NO. ACTUALLY, UM...
I THINK THEY'RE GAS.

405
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,100
GAS? WOW!

406
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:19,687
INTENSE.

407
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,899
IF THIS IS THE WAY
ALL THE GELLERS FLIRT

408
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:24,442
WE DON'T HAVE A PROBLEM.

409
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:30,448
HEY, UH... YOU KNOW
THAT SMELL GAS HAS?

410
00:16:34,828 --> 00:16:35,829
YEAH.

411
00:16:35,829 --> 00:16:38,957
THEY PUT THAT IN.

412
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:40,249
WHAT?

413
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:42,335
THE GAS IS ODORLESS

414
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:44,378
BUT THEY ADD THE SMELL

415
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:47,966
SO YOU KNOW
WHEN THERE'S A LEAK.

416
00:16:49,007 --> 00:16:50,426
WELL, OKAY.

417
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:55,473
A LOT OF
OTHER GAS SMELLS.

418
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,438
OH, THE HUMANITY.

419
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:09,612
ME-METHANE SMELLS.

420
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,030
YOU KNOW WHAT? UM...

421
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,324
ACTUALLY, I...
I REALLY... I SHOULD GO.

422
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:14,826
OH, BUT I-I... I
HAVEN'T PAID YOU YET.

423
00:17:14,826 --> 00:17:16,410
YOU KNOW WHAT?
THAT'S OKAY.

424
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,997
YOU GUYS HAVE ORDERED SO MANY
THAT THIS ONE'S ON ME.

425
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:30,508
WAS I TALKING TO HER ABOUT GAS?

426
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,971
MORE SO THAN
ANYTHING ELSE.

427
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:38,599
I-I... I FOUND
IT INTERESTING.

428
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,896
I'M SORRY.

429
00:17:42,896 --> 00:17:45,648
HEY, HEY,
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

430
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:48,860
IN NINE YEARS,
SHE AND I WILL BE RIGHT THERE.

431
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:58,786
OKAY, WELL, I'M GOING TO
CLEAR OUT SOME OF THESE BOXES.

432
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:06,544
ROSS?
YEAH?

433
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:09,255
WHAT ELSE DO THEY
ADD SMELL TO?

434
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:15,929
CAITLIN.
CAITLIN, HI.

435
00:18:15,929 --> 00:18:18,431
HI, HI, HI. I'M RACHEL.

436
00:18:18,431 --> 00:18:20,516
FROM UPSTAIRS? THE PEOPLE
WITH ALL THE PIZZA?

437
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,268
OH, WAS THERE A PROBLEM?
NO, NO, NO.

438
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,395
EVERYTHING,
THEY'RE FINE. GREAT PIZZA.

439
00:18:24,395 --> 00:18:27,523
BUT IT'S ACTUALLY, UM,
MY FRIEND, ROSS.

440
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:31,694
HE, UH, HE JUST GETS REALLY
NERVOUS WHEN HE'S FLIRTING.

441
00:18:31,694 --> 00:18:33,362
OH, MY GOD.

442
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:34,822
THAT WAS FLIRTING?

443
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,282
YEAH. I KNOW.
WOW.

444
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:37,658
I KNOW. I KNOW.

445
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,035
BUT, UH, JUST...
I'M TELLING YOU.

446
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:41,328
ONCE... ONCE YOU GET
PAST THAT PART

447
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:44,206
WHERE IT JUST FEELS
LIKE YOU WANT TO DIE

448
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:46,542
UM, HE'S... HE'S
A REALLY GOOD PERSON.

449
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,003
THE GUY WITH THE GAS?

450
00:18:49,003 --> 00:18:50,421
YEAH. I-I...
I'M TELLING YOU.

451
00:18:50,421 --> 00:18:52,882
HE'S REALLY SWEET
AND HE'S REALLY FUNNY

452
00:18:52,882 --> 00:18:55,134
AND HE'S JUST...
OH, JUST GOT A GOOD HEART.

453
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:58,178
AND BESIDES, I THINK
HE REALLY LIKES YOU.

454
00:18:58,178 --> 00:18:59,388
REALLY?

455
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,099
YOU KNOW,
WE HAVE SEVEN PEOPLE

456
00:19:01,099 --> 00:19:02,224
AND, LIKE, TEN PIZZAS.

457
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,559
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

458
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:06,562
I JUST... I THOUGHT
JOEY WAS THERE.

459
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:10,399
Man:
You have till Monday

460
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:12,110
then I move to dismiss.

461
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:16,238
HEY, ROSS?

462
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:18,950
UM... I JUST RAN
INTO CAITLIN
IN THE HALLWAY

463
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,035
AND-AND, UH... YOU
MUST BE GETTING BETTER

464
00:19:21,035 --> 00:19:23,121
AT THIS FLIRTING STUFF
THAN I THOUGHT.

465
00:19:23,121 --> 00:19:24,705
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?
WELL, I DON'T GET IT

466
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:28,250
BUT SHE WANTED ME
TO GIVE YOU HER PHONE NUMBER.

467
00:19:32,463 --> 00:19:34,548
AND SHE JUST
GAVE YOU THIS?

468
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,760
YEAH.

469
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:40,680
RACH, THANKS,
BUT I DON'T NEED YOU
DOING ME ANY FAVORS.

470
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,431
I DIDN'T. I DIDN'T.

471
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:45,476
SHE THOUGHT YOU WERE CUTE.

472
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:46,769
WELL, THAT 
I CAN BELIEVE.

473
00:19:46,769 --> 00:19:47,728
YEAH.

474
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:52,066
HEY! IS THE SHOW STILL ON?

475
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:53,818
ALMOST OVER, MAN.

476
00:19:53,818 --> 00:19:55,153
HEY, NONNI.

477
00:19:55,153 --> 00:19:57,822
OH! IS THAT THE POPE?

478
00:19:59,991 --> 00:20:02,284
WHY AM I LOOKING?

479
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:04,704
OH, NONNI, HERE I AM!
LOOK! THIS IS MY BIG SCENE.

480
00:20:04,704 --> 00:20:06,789
All right, back off!

481
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:11,210
Now, I got a gun.

482
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,920
I'm not afraid to use it.

483
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,213
OH, JOEY!

484
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,798
THAT'S RIGHT, NONNI.

485
00:20:15,798 --> 00:20:17,717
YOU COULDN'T HAVE AT LEAST
CHANGED YOUR SHIRT?

486
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:22,930
Now, I want a suitcase
filled with $100,000...

487
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,015
( duck quacking )

488
00:20:24,015 --> 00:20:26,600
Shoo! shoo! shoo!

489
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,227
...filled with $100,000
in small bills.

490
00:20:29,227 --> 00:20:30,229
And if I don't get...
( duck quacking )

491
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:32,190
Shoo!

492
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:35,651
And if I don't get it...

493
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,277
I'm going to shoot this duck!

494
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:38,821
OH, NO!

495
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,158
I'm coming out.

496
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:52,251
AND SHE'S SUPPOSED
TO BUY THIS?

497
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:56,296
JOEY, BRAVO!
BRAVO! BELLISSIMO! OH!

498
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:59,550
Ground Control to Major Tom.

499
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:03,679
Commencing countdown.

500
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:06,140
Engines...

501
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,100
on.

502
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,942
THAT'S, UH, SCENES
FROM NEXT WEEK'S SHOW.

503
00:21:15,942 --> 00:21:18,236
NEXT WEEK.

504
00:21:18,236 --> 00:21:20,947
I AM DEFINITELY
GOING TO WATCH THAT.

505
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:28,537
WHAT ABOUT THESE?
DO THESE LOOK THE SAME?

506
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:29,538
DEFINITELY.

507
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:30,748
NOT AS EACH OTHER.

508
00:21:30,748 --> 00:21:32,666
OH. THEN, NO.

509
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:37,504
HEY, YOU READY?
HI. YEAH.

510
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:38,839
YOU LOOK AMAZING.

511
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,758
I'M THE LUCKIEST MAN
IN THE WORLD.

512
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:43,385
OH, YOU'RE ABOUT TO
GET A LITTLE LUCKIER.

513
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:44,511
LET'S SEE
THE EARRINGS.

514
00:21:44,511 --> 00:21:46,555
OH, RIGHT.
THE EARRINGS.

515
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:48,307
THEY LOOK GREAT.

516
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:52,519
DOES YOUR BOYFRIEND HAVE
THE BEST TASTE OR WHAT?

517
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:56,440
MY BOYFRIEND REALLY
DOES HAVE GREAT TASTE.

518
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:00,945
THANKS FOR PICKING OUT
THE EARRINGS, MAN.
MM-HMM.

